    <!-- Page 7-8: Technology Study -->
    <div class="page">
        <div class="page-header">Cash-Book: Smart Finance &amp; Digital Ledger</div>
        
        <div class="title-box">3. Technology Study</div>
        
        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">❖ React :</div>
        <ul>
            <li>React was first developed by Jordan Walke at Facebook in 2011.</li>
            <li>React is a JavaScript library used for building user interfaces (UI), especially single-page applications (SPA).</li>
            <li>React uses a component-based architecture, where the UI is divided into reusable pieces called components.</li>
            <li>React uses a Virtual DOM to efficiently update only the parts of the page that change, improving performance.</li>
            <li>Vite is used as the build tool, providing a faster and leaner development experience for modern web projects.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">❖ HTML &amp; Tailwind CSS :</div>
        <ul>
            <li>First developed by Tim Berners-Lee in 1990, HTML is short for Hypertext Markup Language.</li>
            <li>HTML is used to create electronic documents (called pages) that are displayed on the World Wide Web.</li>
            <li>Tailwind CSS is a utility-first CSS framework used in this project to rapidly build custom user interfaces without leaving the HTML/JSX.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">❖ JavaScript :</div>
        <ul>
            <li>JavaScript is a dynamic computer programming language.</li>
            <li>It is lightweight and most commonly used as a part of web pages.</li>
            <li>JavaScript allows client-side scripts to interact with the user and fetch dynamic data asynchronously.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">❖ Node.js &amp; Express.js :</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Node.js was developed by Ryan Dahl in 2009.</li>
            <li>It allows running JavaScript outside the browser (on the server side), using the V8 JavaScript engine.</li>
            <li>Express.js is a minimal and flexible Node.js web application framework that provides a robust set of features for web and mobile applications.</li>
            <li>It is used in this project to create RESTful APIs to handle frontend requests securely.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="footer-line" style="position: static;"></div>
        <div class="page-number" style="position: static;">6</div>
    </div>
    
    <!-- Page 9: Technology Study (Cont) -->
    <div class="page">
        <div class="page-header">Cash-Book: Smart Finance &amp; Digital Ledger</div>
        
        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">❖ MongoDB :</div>
        <ul>
            <li>MongoDB was first released in 2009 by MongoDB Inc.</li>
            <li>MongoDB is an open-source NoSQL database.</li>
            <li>It stores data in flexible, JSON-like documents instead of tables, making it perfect for dynamic data models.</li>
            <li>MongoDB is schema-less by nature, though Mongoose is used in this project to enforce structured schemas.</li>
            <li>It is designed for high performance, scalability, and flexibility.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">❖ Development Tools:</div>
        <ul>
            <li><b>VS Code (Visual Studio Code):</b> A free, open-source code editor developed by Microsoft. It is widely used for coding, debugging, and software development.</li>
            <li><b>Postman:</b> Used for API testing and endpoint verification.</li>
            <li><b>Git &amp; GitHub:</b> Used for version control and source code management.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="footer-line" style="position: static;"></div>
        <div class="page-number" style="position: static;">7</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Page 10: Objectives -->
    <div class="page">
        <div class="page-header">Cash-Book: Smart Finance &amp; Digital Ledger</div>
        
        <div class="title-box">4. Objectives</div>
        
        <ul>
            <li>The objective of the project <b>Cash-Book</b> is to design and develop a professional, responsive, and user-friendly web application for personal and small-business finance tracking.</li>
            <li>The platform offers essential features such as transaction logging, categorization, receipt attachments, party ledger for debts/credits, and subscription tracking.</li>
            <li>The aim is to deliver a scalable system that helps users gain complete control and visibility over their financial flow.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-red text-center" style="margin-top: 30px;">Start To End Process</h3>
        
        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">1. Project Planning &amp; Requirement Analysis</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Define the purpose of the website: digital ledger and financial management.</li>
            <li>Identify key features for users: transaction management, dynamic categories, invitations (shared cashbooks), and analytics.</li>
            <li>Finalize the technology stack: React, Tailwind CSS (frontend), Node.js, Express, and MongoDB (backend).</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">2. UI/UX Design</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Design a modern, clean, and responsive dashboard interface.</li>
            <li>Use intuitive color schemes (green for income, red for expense) and high-quality icons.</li>
            <li>Incorporate animations (Framer Motion) to enhance user experience.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">3. Frontend Development</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Use React for building the frontend user interface.</li>
            <li>Build pages such as: Dashboard Home, Transactions, Party Ledger, Receipts Vault, EMI Tracker, and Settings.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="footer-line" style="position: static;"></div>
        <div class="page-number" style="position: static;">8</div>
    </div>

    <!-- Page 11: Objectives Cont -->
    <div class="page">
        <div class="page-header">Cash-Book: Smart Finance &amp; Digital Ledger</div>
        
        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">4. Backend Development</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Use Node.js with Express.js to handle user authentication, transaction logic, and data aggregation.</li>
            <li>Connect to MongoDB via Mongoose for managing backend data like:
                <ul>
                    <li>Users</li>
                    <li>Transactions and Cashbooks</li>
                    <li>Categories and Payment Modes</li>
                    <li>Invitations and Receipts</li>
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li>Implement secure authentication (JWT) for API protection.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">5. Functionality Implementation</div>
        <ul>
            <li><b>User Side:</b> Registration/Login, add/edit/delete transactions, filter by date/category, manage debts, view graphical reports.</li>
            <li><b>Admin Side:</b> System analytics, manage all users, oversee total transactions across the platform.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="sub-title" style="display: block; text-align: center;">6. Testing &amp; Optimization</div>
        <ul>
            <li>Perform end-to-end testing of form validations, API response times, and state management.</li>
            <li>Optimize UI rendering using React hooks and lazy loading components.</li>
        </ul>
        
        <div class="footer-line" style="position: static;"></div>
        <div class="page-number" style="position: static;">9</div>
    </div>

